1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,070
Listen to a teacher talking in a social studies class.

2
00:00:03,070 --> 00:00:06,200
Have you ever thought about the games that people played hundreds of years ago?

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:11,190
In the Middle Ages, people often got together and competed in various folk games.

4
00:00:11,190 --> 00:00:15,180
They would form teams and kick around a ball or some round object.

5
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:20,240
The objective of a folk game was most often to move the ball to some fixed point and score points.

6
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:23,337
Sounds a lot like modem games, doesn’t it?

7
00:00:23,337 --> 00:00:26,090
But in actuality, folk games were much different !

8
00:00:26,090 --> 00:00:30,200
One big difference is that nowadays the rules of such games are written down.

9
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:33,589
Each game has a specific clear set of rules that you can look up

10
00:00:33,589 --> 00:00:36,010
and consult when you’re not sure what to do.

11
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:40,020
In the past, though, very few people who played these games could even read.

12
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:44,060
So they simply memorized the rules and passed them down by tradition.

13
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:48,511
Also, the teams that played in folk games were nothing like the carefully structured

14
00:00:48,511 --> 00:00:50,100
teams in today’s games.

15
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:53,328
Today，each player has a specific role.Like in soccer,

16
00:00:53,328 --> 00:00:56,556
when one player’s job is to protect the goal,

17
00:00:56,556 --> 00:00:58,170
and others try to score.

18
00:00:58,170 --> 00:01:01,230
There's a lot of specialization in roles and positions.

19
00:01:01,230 --> 00:01:05,300
But in the past, folk games were played more like children play games today.

20
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,361
Think about how kids usually play a game:

21
00:01:08,361 --> 00:01:11,040
they will often change positions or roles.

22
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:16,401
This is more or less how teams were organized in the past.And another difference,

23
00:01:16,401 --> 00:01:19,260
nowadays, sports games are considered very positive activities.

24
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:26,130
They keep you healthy and they teach teamwork.But folk games of the past were not regarded so positively.

25
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:28,052
They were often played in the streets,

26
00:01:28,052 --> 00:01:32,170
and to a lot of people, they looked more like scary riots than sport events!

27
00:01:32,170 --> 00:01:36,178
The games were very rowdy and often ended in broken windows

28
00:01:36,178 --> 00:01:38,000
or other damage to property.

29
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,591
In fact, folk games were considered so primitive that authorities in some places even

30
00:01:42,591 --> 00:01:44,230
tried to ban them completely.

31
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:48,936
For example, in medieval England, authorities tried up to 30 times to stop such

32
00:01:48,936 --> 00:01:50,280
contests from being organized.

33
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:51,647
But it didn't work.

34
00:01:51,647 --> 00:01:56,090
People continued to play these games in the streets for hundreds of years.
